| 1 | Seam Map | weak | 8 | 40 | Risklytics already sells policy-gap analysis ([interview](https://datainnovation.org/2026/07/5-qs-with-samuel-gold-founder-of-risklytics/)); gap analysis is free commentary from coverage counsel ([Fenwick](https://fenwick.com/insights/publications/end-silent-ai-emerging-ai-exclusions-coverage-fragmentation-and-practical-implications), [Haynes Boone](https://www.haynesboone.com/news/alerts/ai-exclusions-in-insurance-policies-what-to-do)); only "a few carriers" attach so far ([Insurance Business](https://www.businessinsurance.com/insurers-brokers-adjust-as-ai-exclusions-emerge/)) |
| 2 | Warranty File | weak | 5 | 45 | Evidence layer already built by Drata (native AIUC-1, [post](https://drata.com/blog/introducing-aiuc-1)) and SafeBase ([post](https://www.safebase.io/blog/introducing-aiuc-1)); verification startups exist ([IntellectAI, Coalition, Cyberwrite](https://fintech.global/2026/07/22/how-ai-can-rescue-cyber-submissions-from-the-black-hole/)); insured-side $3k/yr exceeds any plausible premium discount; Travelers v. ICS ended with rescission stipulated, but it is one case ([Inside Privacy](https://www.insideprivacy.com/data-security/cybersecurity/cyber-insurer-seeks-to-void-data-breach-coverage-because-of-purported-misstatements-in-policy-application/)) |
