| 4 | Gate Meter | weak | 8 | 70 | Telemetry-priced AI cover is an obvious idea (arXiv [2606.16465](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.16465), [2607.11999](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.11999)), and Mount already pairs red-teaming with pricing ([YC](https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/mount)); AIUC-1 already specifies execution-chain logs as underwriting evidence; no gateway vendor has an insurer tie-in, which is a gap but also a sign of a weak channel |
| 5 | Waive List | weak | 5 | 45 | No source that treaties force blanket attachment; underwriters simply ask which models insureds use (Westfield quoted in [Insurance Business](https://www.businessinsurance.com/insurers-brokers-adjust-as-ai-exclusions-emerge/)); CyberCube/Kovrr/Cytora/Kalepa/Sixfold already sit in the intake path; the author's own ceiling is $40-70M |
